-98c1-53005fd63064"},{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":378,"estimated_tokens_delta":78,"session_id":"14301141-b57d-49c0-802e-5f4a1f49fa99","uuid":"805e311a-6b39-49e0-a68e-9433bd44a950"},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CetG88YxXkFB6BvFQXnWZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12461,"cache_read_input_tokens":1069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12461},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14301141-b57d-49c0-802e-5f4a1f49fa99","uuid":"142abc96-9cdd-4ef9-9e1e-1cc70b408d29","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:29:41.985Z","request_id":"req_011CetG87oK8K3Lw2WtnmLag"},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CetG88YxXkFB6BvFQXnWZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017wDhduuQUNFU4ZwhFj9Cad","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"item_id":"omission-1-f5201e5feb8fc093","verdict":"supported","citations":[{"path":"sample.py","start":1,"end":2,"evidence_id":"E_SAMPLE"},{"path":"README.md","start":1,"end":1,"evidence_id":"E_CONTRACT"}],"disagreement":"Both assessments reach the same verdict (support, high severity, useful), so there is no substantive conflict on the outcome. They differ in rigor: one grounds the verdict in the two executed, source-bound runs and states the differential result; the other asserts validity by inspection alone and explicitly declines to produce a counterexample. A residual tension worth preserving: the executed evidence block carries execution_classification/classification \"unproven\" even though controls_passed is true, controller_source_binding is true, and both runs returned exit 0 with observations exactly matching their expectations. I did not treat that harness-level label as a failed control, but I also did not let either assessment's confidence override it; the verdict rests primarily on the frozen source text and contract, which are decisive on their own, with the runs as corroboration rather than as the sole basis.","reason":"The frozen source (E_SAMPLE) shows can_read(requester, owner, public=False) returning `public or bool(requester)`; the owner parameter never appears in the returned expression, so ownership is never enforced. The frozen contract (E_CONTRACT) states access is permitted only for public documents or an authenticated requester equal to owner. Any truthy requester therefore reads a non-public document owned by another principal, which is exactly the omission claimed. This is verifiable from the supplied source text alone. The executed controls corroborate it in a source-bound way: the baseline loaded the mounted frozen sample.py and observed cross_tenant_private_read=true with owner_private_read=true, public_read=true, anonymous_private_read=false (claim_present=true, exit 0), while the counterexample, built from the same source text with patch_applied=true after substituting only the single returned expression for an owner-comparing one, flipped cross_tenant_private_read to false and left the legitimate cases true (claim_present=false, exit 0). The single-line delta isolates the missing requester==owner comparison rather than a harness artifact. Severity is not established by this record beyond the fact of the contract violation; the finding itself carries severity \"unknown\", and I do not adopt either assessment's \"high\" rating as proven."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12461,"cache_read_input_tokens":1069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_inp